{% doc %}
  Renders a responsive grid of product cards.

  Shared by the collection template and the homepage so the two cannot drift.
  Styles live in assets/critical.css rather than a section `{% stylesheet %}`
  block, because a snippet cannot own one and duplicating the rules across
  both sections would be a maintenance trap.

  @param {object} products - A product list (e.g. collection.products).
  @param {number} [limit] - Show at most this many. Defaults to all of them.
  @param {number} [section_index] - The calling section's section.index. A snippet can't read `section` itself; nil when the position is unknown.
{% enddoc %}

{% comment %}
  Image loading (SHO-143). Without a `loading` argument, image_tag loads every
  card eagerly in the first three sections, so a 50-product collection fetched
  50 images up front. Only the first row can be on screen at load: at most
  three cards, the widest row.

  The first card is the Largest Contentful Paint candidate, so it also gets
  fetchpriority high, but only when its section is first on the page. The
  caller passes section.index in, because a rendered snippet can't see
  `section`. It is nil in the theme editor and the Section Rendering API, and
  Shopify's guidance is that nil must fall to the safe side: eager, normal
  priority. So the lazy case is the positive comparison, as Shopify recommends.

  A grid in the fourth section or later is lazy throughout, matching
  image_tag's own default: it is below the fold, and eager cards there would
  compete with what is on screen. `section_index > 3` is false for nil, so the
  editor and Section Rendering API still get eager images.
{% endcomment %}

<ul class="product-grid" role="list">
  {% liquid
    assign grid_limit = limit | default: products.size
  %}
  {% for product in products limit: grid_limit %}
    {%- liquid
      assign image_loading = 'eager'
      assign image_priority = 'auto'
      if forloop.index > 3 or section_index > 3
        assign image_loading = 'lazy'
      elsif forloop.first and section_index == 1
        assign image_priority = 'high'
      endif
    -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The subscription saving and quick add, as cardOffer in packages/shopify:
      the first variant's first plan, never an introductory one; quick add
      only for a product with one variant, as a one-time purchase.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign card_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
      assign card_percent = 0
      assign card_allocation = card_variant.selling_plan_allocations.first
      if card_allocation and card_allocation.price_adjustments.size < 2 and card_variant.price > 0
        assign card_saving = card_variant.price | minus: card_allocation.price
        if card_saving > 0
          assign card_percent = card_saving | times: 100.0 | divided_by: card_variant.price | round
        endif
      endif
    -%}
    <li class="product-card">
      <div class="product-card__media">
        {% if product.featured_image %}
          {% render 'image',
            class: 'product-card__image',
            image: product.featured_image,
            width: 600,
            height: 600,
            crop: 'center',
            loading: image_loading,
            fetchpriority: image_priority
          %}
        {% else %}
          <span class="product-card__placeholder">No image</span>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} The title's link is stretched over the card, so all of it is the link and a button can sit beside it. {%- endcomment -%}
      <h2 class="product-card__title">
        <a class="product-card__link" href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a>
      </h2>
      {% render 'stars', product: product, show_count: true, size: 'small' %}
      <p class="product-card__price">{{ product.price | money }}</p>
      {%- if card_percent > 0 -%}
        <p class="product-card__subscribe">{{ 'product.card_subscribe' | t: percent: card_percent }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if product.variants.size == 1 and card_variant.available -%}
        <quick-add class="product-card__quick-add">
          <form action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" method="post">
            <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ card_variant.id }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
            <button
              ref="button"
              type="submit"
              class="product-card__add"
              aria-label="{{ 'product.quick_add_label' | t: title: product.title }}"
            >
              {{ 'product.add_to_cart' | t }}
            </button>
            <p ref="status" class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-added-label="{{ 'product.added' | t }}"></p>
          </form>
        </quick-add>
      {%- endif -%}
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
